maluos-system-monitor (49.1+maluos.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The self-test no longer fails while a GetState call is still in flight:
    on a slow machine (the boot test under TCG) the window's first paint held
    the main loop past the 20 s deadline and the timer fired before the
    reply was dispatched. The deadline is now 60 s, a pending call is always
    waited for (the call's own 30 s timeout ends it), a refused call fails
    the test at once, and the FAIL line carries the D-Bus error.
  * The gsettings schema accepts `gpus` for current-tab, so the GPUs tab is
    remembered like the others (no "outside of valid range" warning).

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0000

maluos-system-monitor (49.1+maluos.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * GNOME System Monitor 49.1 (Ubuntu 26.04's 49.1-2 packaging) forked for
    MaluOS, Phase 13 shared GPUs slice G1 (docs/phase13-shared-gpus.md):
    the GPUs tab (src/maluos-gpus.cpp), fed by the MaluOS session service
    over D-Bus and acting only through `pkexec maluctl gateway share`;
    `--show-gpus-tab` and `--maluos-self-test`; Alt+4. The patch surface
    is listed in README.maluos.md. Replaces gnome-system-monitor.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:45:00 +0000
